# 16. Tattva 10: Kāla — sequential time

Universal nonsequential presence becomes:

[
T_\infty
\rightarrow
(t_1,t_2,\ldots,t_n).
]

The local subject inhabits temporal succession:

* retention of the past;
* current presence;
* anticipation of the future.

