# 17. Tattva 11: Niyati — causal and situational placement

Niyati restricts omnipresence and unrestricted possibility.

A finite subject is here rather than everywhere, under these conditions rather than all conditions.

Formally:

[
C_i
===

{\text{initial conditions, causal neighbourhood, embodiment, history}}.
]

## Inexternalist reconstruction

Niyati is indexical causal location:

[
\boxed{
\text{this body},
\quad
\text{this history},
\quad
\text{this environment},
\quad
\text{these constraints}.
}
]

It contributes directly to phenomenal privacy.

Another organism’s state is excluded because it belongs to a different:

* causal trajectory;
* sensory access structure;
* memory network;
* regulatory closure;
* embodied location.

This gives a scientific account of why:

[
D_i\neq D_j.
]

But causal separation alone does not explain why either system is manifest.

Niyati explains partition conditions.

It does not yet prove phenomenal partition.

