# PART THREE — THE COGNITIVE AND EMBODIED TATTVAS

# 19. Tattva 13: Prakṛti — the organized field of finite nature

Prakṛti supplies the differentiated resources of embodied cognition.

In Sāṅkhya, prakṛti is independent of puruṣa.

In Trika it is ultimately another articulation of conscious power.

## Inexternalist reconstruction

Prakṛti is the organism–environment state space available to the local subject:

[
\mathcal X_i
============

\mathcal X_{\text{body}}
\times
\mathcal X_{\text{brain}}
\times
\mathcal X_{\text{environment}}.
]

It contains the dynamical resources from which:

* cognition;
* affect;
* sensation;
